d. acts violating decency that are contrary to the will of the victim and religious values recognized in Indonesia;
e. pornography involving Children or pornography that explicitly contains violence and sexual exploitation;
f. forced prostitution;
g. criminal acts of human trafficking intended for sexual exploitation;
h. sexual violence within the domestic sphere;
i. criminal acts of money laundering where the predicate offense constitutes a Sexual Violence Criminal Act; and
j. other criminal acts expressly stated as Sexual Violence Criminal Acts as regulated in the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 19
(1) In the framework of providing protection services to women and children from acts of violence, the Regional Government establishes UPTDPPA.
(2) UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1), functions to implement services for:
a. public complaints;
b. victim outreach;
c. case management;
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; and
f. victim assistance.
(3) Further provisions regarding the organization and work procedures of UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by a Regent Regulation.
